  "id": "COMPOUND:20231 - PROTEIN:6319",
  "verbalization": "Halocynthiaxanthin is shown to have a target relationship with UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4 through multiple pathways. The first path links Halocynthiaxanthin to WRL68, which in turn is targeted by a long-chain peptide and ultimately targets UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4. The second and third paths similarly connect Halocynthiaxanthin to Disintegrin and metalloproteinase domain-containing protein 9, which is also targeted by a complex molecule and ultimately targets UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4. These findings suggest that Halocynthiaxanthin may exert its effects through a common mechanism involving the regulation of UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4, potentially through direct interaction or indirect modulation of the target protein. The evidence supports a plausible biological relationship, but further investigation is needed to confirm the exact mechanism of action and the role of Halocynthiaxanthin in modulating this enzyme.",
